    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "The Content Management System (CMS) integration pattern addresses how content editors manage translations at scale. Rather than editing JSON or YAML files directly, professional translation workflows use Translation Management Systems (TMS) like Phrase, Lokalise, or Crowdin. These platforms provide interfaces for translators, track translation progress, maintain translation memory, and integrate with version control systems. The technical implementation typically involves webhooks or API integrations that pull new translations into your application's build pipeline. This architecture separates content management from code deployment, enabling translations to be updated without code changes while maintaining version control for auditability."
